vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T19:56:43-08:00","id":1503874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1503873#post1503873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, I don't like this merit, but I think it can be salvaged by using it somewhere else. Up to you to use if you think it fits. If you want to use it, I'd say instead of a Soul Stone, use a bit of Iron, or Cold Iron for a bonus, and you can clash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good, I'll hammer something out with that. Thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1503873#post1503873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...yeah.<br /> The wording is kind of vague, and I think could be used to return from a pocket dimension or the underworld or somthing...Which seems way out of the scope of merit. If that's the intended use... How in the world is that Mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: I <i>think</i> &quot;supernatural experience that separates him from reality&quot; just means hallucinations and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-24-2023, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T11:03:06-08:00","id":1503906,"title":"","content":"I think it would be interesting if the phylactery was inspired by <i>The Portrait of Dorian Gray</i>, created at the Goblin Market by making a specially prepared painting into a Soul Stone. Every revival could accrue a point of Goblin Debt. Rather than high amounts of debt transforming a mage into a goblin, it would instead bind them to a Painting/Mirror Person Familiar (meaning they can Discorporate and reform as the painting's image) that would pursue certain Wyrd chosen goals to settle the debt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-25-2023, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T15:19:59-08:00","id":1503916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1503906#post1503906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be interesting if the phylactery was inspired by <i>The Portrait of Dorian Gray</i>, created at the Goblin Market by making a specially prepared painting into a Soul Stone. Every revival could accrue a point of Goblin Debt. Rather than high amounts of debt transforming a mage into a goblin, it would instead bind them to a Painting/Mirror Person Familiar (meaning they can Discorporate and reform as the painting's image) that would pursue certain Wyrd chosen goals to settle the debt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, you mean make it into a Lich Legacy? Or the Fetchling is able to resurrect itself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T15:55:45-08:00","id":1503917,"title":"","content":"I wasn't thinking of a Legacy, however, that is an interesting idea. I meant starting with the Mirror People from page 267 of the CofD book, give it the Immortal Dread Power as a base and then build it so the image in the portrait becomes their Mr Hyde, serving the Wyrd's/Goblin's agenda. I think it could lead to an interesting Mystery, especially if there is some kind of reason to prevent them from revealing the situation, all while dealing with the fallout of the doppleganger's actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T09:17:53-08:00","id":1503948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1503714#post1503714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What spells would be needed for a Legacy aping Changelings? The gouges caused by Thorns could certainly be tempting Mysteries for a reckless Mage to make something out of. I can repurpose parts of my Hedgemarshals, but they're focused on being bountryhunters. I want someone who's whole shtick is wanting to be a Changeling without most of the downsides.<br /> <br /> I assume it would be a Fate-primary Legacy, since Fate seems to be the dominant Arcana over Mind when it comes to Changling-adjascent spells.<br /> <br /> <b>Courtiers of the Thorn Brand</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames</b>: Courtlings, Hedgewalkers, Thornweavers, Keeperlings (Derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> lalala [Friendly with Changelings and try to get Goodwill with as many courts as possible. Fate-Masters are often welcomed as brokers for strange contracts, but Second-Degree Legacy Masters are side-eyed for their &quot;Fetchlings&quot;]<br /> <br /> <b>Theory:</b> Just because magic isn't Supernal, doesn't mean it isn't a route to enlightenment. The Exarchs broke the world to secure their dominion, and it would be foolish to ignore the fragments other than our own.<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Lalala [Founded by a Mage who went Rapt studying the ragged state of Changeling souls, creating a Legacy that emulated the gouges in a more artistic form. Several would-be students attempted to learn from his Soul Stone and went Rapt themselves before a one managed to puzzle out a stable form.]<br /> <br /> <b>Parentage:</b> Free Council, Mastigos<br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcana</b>: Fate<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Lalala<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Assisting with Court Bargain rituals; Safely traversing the Hedge; Performing a favor for a Hedge denizen without seeking recompense; Triggering an event that would net Glamour if the Mage were a Changeling<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><i>Keen Periphery 2</i><i>, Piercing Glance 2</i><br /> <b>Initiation: </b>There are two common methods of initiation into the Courtlings. The first -and most common- is to closely study the soul of a Changeling, identifying the various cuts and scrapes that have elevated the fairy to something more than human. This is best performed on a willing subject, although that is far from required. The prospective Initiate is then walked through the proper pattern to carve by their mentor, carefully working to avoid the slips that will send the Mage into Rapture.<br /> <br /> The second method is to willingly walk into the Thorns of the Hedge, wandering its depths until the briar has gouged out alien geometries upon Gnosis. While the far riskier method, initiates of this method often emerge bearing strange Artifacts, Tokens, or novel Attainments.<br /> <br /> <b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe Form Of A Thing </b><br /> (Fate \u25cf) <i>Initiation</i><br /> Though their glance cannot see through all illusions, the Courtling is innured enough to the tides of Arcadia to see through Arcadian Masks.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">An always-on effect that allows the mage to see through Masks as if they were Fae<br /> <br /> Commentary: Eh. Not much to say. Basically a convenience thing, not needing Active Mage Sight up.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> (Mind \u25cf)<br /> A strange truth can be found in the surety of iron - that all illusions are as fleeting as the wind. Using cold iron in hand to draw hot iron from their own veins, the Courtling rages against perceived intrusions. Should this lashing out prove accurate, the drawn blood bubbles away as an iridescent smoke.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Emulates the Epiphany Stone merit, but cuts themself with a piece of iron rather than utilizes a Soul Stone. This deals one point of Resistant Bashing Damage.<br /> <br /> Commentary: an... odd effect, suggested by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26736_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26736\" data-vbnamecard=\"26736\">TempleBuilder</a>. Could replace it with giving the Mage a Glamour pool... although the closest equivalent would be <u>Mana Battery</u>, which is Disciple level.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>The Intangibles</b><br /> (Fate \u25cf\u25cf) <i>Piercing Glance 4</i><br /> The Wyrd is not quite the threads of Fate, and not quite the bonds of Sympathy, yet there is a kinship there nonetheless. The marks the Courtling etched into themself blur the distinctions between those gossamer weavings.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u>Interconnections</u><br /> Potency = Fate<br /> Duration = Two Turns<br /> Scale = 1 Subject, 2 Subjects at Fate 4<br /> Range = Sight<br /> Casting Time = Instant<br /> <br /> Commentary: Spot them tricksy oathbreakers. At the Adept level, you can even discern the connections between subjects two at a time.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> (Mind \u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Something in the scouring that shapes Changelings opens them to the currents of emotion in other entities. Carefully trimming at the edges of their Gnosis in imitation, the Courtling is able to glean similar details.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u>Mental Scan</u><br /> Potency = Mind<br /> Duration = Two Turns<br /> Scale = 1 Subject, 2 Subjects at Mind 4<br /> Withstand = Composure<br /> Range = Sight<br /> Casting Time = Instant (Reach to Instant Casting)<br /> NOTE: Activates simultaneously with the Fate portion of the Attainment. This is not optional. Prioritizes emotional state, then psychosis, then desires, then Mage's choice.<br /> <br /> Commentary: Not exactly mind-reading, but still useful. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Between What You Can Touch</b><br /> (Fate \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) <i>\u200bIt's Only A Weave 2, Astral Adept 3</i><br /> Though creating new Hedge Irises requires Mastery of Fate, an experienced Courtling can leverage their understanding of the superficially-similar Astral to rip open pre-existing Hedgeways with but a flicker of will.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u>Open Hedgegate</u><br /> Duration = Fate<br /> Potency = N/A (2, 3 at Fate 4)<br /> Range = Touch<br /> Casting Time = Instant (Reach to Instant Casting\u200b)<br /> <br /> Commentary: <i>Spotting</i> Hedgegates might be a bit tricky, but you can sure as heck guarentee they'll open to you.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> (Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> While not quite as mutable as the Astral, the Hedge has a plasticity that responds nicely to Awakened will. A Courtling hones this control to a knife-fine edge, albeit one that requires constant attention.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u>Malleable Thorns</u><br /> Potency = Mind<br /> Duration = Two Turns, Three Turns at Mind 4<br /> Range = Self/Touch<br /> Casting Time = Instant (Reach to Instant Casting) NOTE: Reach to Paradigm Shift. Mage can now purchase Hedgespinning-related Merits.<br /> <br /> Commentary: Powerful and spam-able, but you'll need to act fast.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>And What You Can't</b>\u200b<br /> (Fate \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) <i>Supernal Taxonomy 2</i><i>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1500556#post1500556\">Vagaries Of Fate</a> 1, Occult 4</i><br /> There is a faction within the Adamant Arrow who believe that any oath -even those not backed by some form of magic- contains a spark of the Supernal. While the Courtlings cannot speak to mundane oaths, they can certainly attest to the power of oaths sworn beneath the aegis of the Wyrd. They have studied the nature of such pacts so closely that a reflection has taken root within them.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u>Wyrd-backed Oath</u><br /> Duration = Lasting<br /> Potency = N/A (3)<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bRange = Self<br /> Casting Time = N/A (Scene)<br /> NOTE: Gives bonus benefit of being able to buy <u>Court Goodwill</u> dots as if the Mage was a Changeling. When this Attainment is first learned, any dots of the <u>Ally</u> merit relating to Changeling Courts that the Mage possesses are automatically converted into the equivalent number of <u>Court Goodwill</u> dots. <u>Court Goodwill</u> also expands the Courtling's Legacy Oblations to include Court-based methods of Glamour harvest based on their <u>Court Goodwill</u>.<br /> <br /> Commentary: Not <i>hugely</i> useful as an Attainment, especially an Adept-level one, but it saves on casting and the Mantle bit can be a nice bit of flavor.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> (Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> The Courtlings willingly step into a realm woven of barely-contained madness, sculpt their soul in emulation of the wounds that realm can inflict, and engage in rituals that border on manias. To engage in such hubris and emerge at least sane enough to continue functioning, the Courtling's mind raises a bulwark of pure will.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u>Mental Shield</u><br /> Potency = Mind<br /> Duration = One Week (Reach to Advanced Duration)<br /> Range = Self<br /> Casting Time = Instant (Reach to Instant Casting)<br /> NOTE: Reach to switch Potency to Primary Factor<br /> <br /> Commentary: Simple. Basic. Actually, pretty powerful. Withstand 5 is nothing to sniff at.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>It's The Nature Of A Thing</b><br /> (Fate \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) <i>\u200bHob Kin 1, Occult 5</i><br /> A Courtling Master has blurred the line between Mage and Changeling, and knows on a fundamental level that it is not the form of a thing that matters, but it's nature. All things are symbols, you simply need the proper cypher to interface with foreign symbols. Drawing deep on this understanding, the Courtling weaves strange new bonds between the writhing fragments of the Fallen World.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u>Masking the False Fae</u><br /> Duration = Indefinite (Two Reach to Indefinite Duration)<br /> Potency = 3<br /> Range = Touch<br /> Withstand = Resolve<br /> Cost = 1 Mana<br /> Casting Time = Scene<br /> NOTE: Conditional Duration [Entity attacks -or is attacked by- a petitioner]. If the Mage reaches the Adept level of understanding in Mind, Spirit, or Death, entities that fall under the auspices of that Arcana become valid targets.<br /> <br /> Commentary: Not very impressive for a Master slot on the face of it, but holy heck they'd be in demand to broker contracts.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> (Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> The Courtling rummages through the Hedge, snatching up sticks, stones, scaps, and dross. Cobbling together an artistic representation of a creature as fantastical as they please, they infuse their &quot;Effegy&quot; with a flicker of Glamour-flavored Mana to give it life. The Mana draws substance from the fabric of the Hedge, creating a life-sized entity in emulation of the Effegy. These &quot;Fetchlings&quot; are Hobs for all intents and purposes, albeit Hobs who feel an instinctive loyalty towards the Courtling. Fetchlings will last for as long as their Effegy remains intact, and as such become very protective of them.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Create Fetchling [Golem]</u><br /> Potency = Mind<br /> Duration = Indefinite (Two Reach to Indefinite Duration)<br /> Scale = Up to Size 5<br /> Range = Touch<br /> Cost = 1 Mana<br /> Casting Time = Scene<br /> NOTE: Conditional Duration [The Fetchling's Effegy is destroyed]. Can only be activated Hedge. Effegy can be sculpture, drawing, painting, carving, or the like, but must be a visual representation and no smaller than a handspan.<br /> <br /> Commentary: Make li'l minions. Whether they can teach Goblin Contracts is another matter.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u>It's Only A Weave</u> (\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <i>Prerequisites</i>: Fate \u25cf\u25cf, Mind \u25cf\u25cf<br /> <i>Description</i>:<br /> The Mage has become an expert at traversing The Hedge, and can navigate it as if they were a Changeling. The Mage substitutes Gnosis for Wyrd where appropriate, and Wisdom for Clarity<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Changling-adjascent spells</b><br /> 1. Break Boundary<br /> 2. Dream Reaching<br /> 3. Interconnections<br /> 4. Correspondence<br /> 5. Sworn Oaths<br /> 6. Malleable Thorns<br /> 7. Open Hedgegate<br /> 8. Create Hedgegate<br /> 9. Channel Glamour<br /> 10. Harvest Glamour<br /> 11. Wyrd-backed Oath<br /> 12. Masking the False Fae<br /> 13. Sleep of the Just<br /> 14. Mend Clarity<br /> 15. Knit Clarity<br /> 16. Fabricate Fortune<br /> 17. Alter Mental Pattern<br /> 18. Emotional Urging<br /> 19. Clear Thoughts<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Another possible approach could be Fate and Spirit. Since the Exarchs supposedly broke the Hedge, they theorize the tales are not flowing in the proper direction. So they shift the context and the emotional resonance of the myths back in the right direction, by shifting the intent of the tale, Materializing the right props, redefining the constraints the actors are under, making sure Fate lets them flow in the right direction. They are prompters and stagehands, the most revered masters are choreographers. The danger and Hubris comes from not only taking responsibility for all the actors, but also contending with countermoves of the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-26-2023, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T02:56:42-08:00","id":1504347,"title":"","content":"More or less done with the Courtlings, although if anyone can recommend polish-points I'd appreciate it. They need a better name though, anyone have suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T17:03:47-08:00","id":1504516,"title":"","content":"Sooo... the whole thread goes down if I update the index post. Gooooood to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T17:10:56-08:00","id":1504517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1504516#post1504516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo... the whole thread goes down if I update the index post. Gooooood to know.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a lesson I had to learn with the Whiskey, Gin, and Teeth thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T16:06:48-08:00","id":1505066,"title":"","content":"Unflagged! Huzzah.<br /> <br /> In the interim, I updated the Iron Tower a bit: their Adept Attainments got a polish to make them more streamlined, and I ended up replacing the Disciple Attainments wholesale. Not hugely happy that I've now made them bruisers, but I think it overall follows a better arc of progression.<br /> <br /> Also still soliciting better names for the Courtlings. &quot;Courtiers of the Thorn Brand&quot; doesn't exactly flow off the tongue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T17:19:06-08:00","id":1505074,"title":"","content":"Jewelers of the Jade Maze ? Jade slips are normally used as magical items in xianxia, plus the Hedge itself is being forged into these items, which has the associated color. It covertly alludes to the origin and magical nature of the items, at least enough to pick the context clues with an Occult roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T05:18:40-08:00","id":1505106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1505074#post1505074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jewelers of the Jade Maze ? Jade slips are normally used as magical items in xianxia, plus the Hedge itself is being forged into these items, which has the associated color. It covertly alludes to the origin and magical nature of the items, at least enough to pick the context clues with an Occult roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good suggestion, though I'll need to change the founder's Shadow Names. Surtr and Morrigan don't quite seem like the kind of names you'd associate with xianxia. Probably change Surtr's sword into a chisel too, to match the &quot;Jeweler&quot; bit...<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's an unrelated Imbued Item.<br /> <br /> <b>Imbued Item</b>: Westphall's Snowglobe (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Effects</b>: Secret Room (Space \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf), Alter Direction (Space \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Mana Cost:</b> 2<br /> <b>Mana Reservoir:</b> 1<br /> <b>Activation</b>: Persistent<br /> <b>Reach</b>: Indefinite Duration<br /> <b>Other Traits:</b> No Flexible Reach, Relinquished, Everywhere, Combined Spell<br /> <br /> A curio in many ways, and difficult to replicate due to the needed understanding of Space, Prime, and Matter, Westphall's Snowglobe is a portable Sanctum. Looking from the outside like nothing more than a palm-sized snowglobe containing a highly detailed castle, discerning eyes might notice that there is no liquid or &quot;snow&quot; within. Further, careful study will soon reveal a small, complex, and well crafted hatch on the globe's brass base.<br /> <br /> Passing through this hatch -impossible without the use of spells such as <u>Break Boundary</u> or <u>Teleport</u>- reveals a well-appointed and vaguely steampunk entry hall, which in turn leads to a grand marble staircase. Ascending these steps bring the visitor into the castle proper, a perfectly constructed domicile that can house dozens of people comfortably. Originally <u>Shaped</u> of plaster and Lastingly reinforced by copious castings of <u>Alter Integrity</u>, the castle is fully decorated with simple furniture of high quality. However, residents will need to be creative for mundane tasks such as cooking or ablutions, as there is no plumbing or electrical systems. Spacious gardens of real loam extend around the castle proper, their quality and crops depending on how well the current owner tends them.<br /> <br /> The interior of the Snowglobe is a &quot;massive&quot; space created through the Secret Room spell. The entire area remains perfectly balanced through the use of the <u>Alter Direction </u>spell, keeping the direction of &quot;up&quot; fixed on the peak of the Snowglobe's dome.<br /> <br /> Many have owned the globe over the years, with various levels of care given to it's upkeep. Careless owners, for example, have often forgotten that plants need sunlight and left the orb to languish on shelves or in storerooms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 03-11-2023, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T07:47:19-08:00","id":1505116,"title":"","content":"Somehow, this makes me visualize one of its owners having built a room inside for their snowglobe collection, where each snowglobe was filled by utilizing a Making of Space and Time to store copies of their favorite moments in history. Like a more festive version of Trazyn The Infinite's archive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T01:57:35-07:00","id":1506466,"title":"","content":"As mught be expected from nascent godlings, Mages have a tendency to recreate mythological artifacts and items of myth. The Gjallarhorn is one such item, seeing several variants in circulation amongst Asatru enthusiasts and dedicated warriors.<br /> <br /> <b>Imbued Item</b>: &quot;The&quot; Gjallarhorn, AKA The Iron Gjallarhorn (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Effects</b>: Golem (Matter \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf), &quot;Forces - Mutable Mask&quot; (Forces \u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Mana Cost</b>: 2<br /> <b>Mana Reservoir</b>: 1<br /> <b>Activation</b>: Contingent (The horn is sounded)<br /> <b>Reach</b>: Instant Casting<br /> <b>Other Traits: </b>No Flexible Reach, Relinquished, Everywhere, Permanence, Combined Spell<br /> <br /> A variant popular in Matter-heavy Consilli, this Gjallarhorn is a curved war-horn wrought of fine steel and etched with Elder Futhark runes. When blown, it animates any humanoid structures within a [Scale] area around the sounder. These golems converge on the hornsounder and follow her orders to the letter. The golems also gain a simple Forces illusion as they come to life, causing them to appear as armored vikings. The most pragmatic owners will ensure they have a stable of suitable subjects on hand to animate, an army in effegy prepared to march at the horn's call.<br /> <br /> A vanishingly rare version of this Gjallarhorn has a Mind component, creating highly intelligent units of golems to serve the hornsounder. <hr /><br /> <b>Imbued Item</b>: &quot;The&quot; Gjallarhorn, AKA The Ivory Gjallarhorn (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Effects</b>: Quicken Corpse (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf), Corpse Mask (Death \u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Mana Cost</b>: 3<br /> <b>Mana Reservoir</b>: 3<br /> <b>Activation</b>: Contingent (The horn is sounded)<br /> <b>Reach</b>: Advanced Duration, &quot;Super Zombies&quot; Reach Effect<br /> <b>Other Traits</b>: No Flexible Reach, Relinquished, Everywhere, Time In A Bottle, Combined Spell<br /> <br /> A highly morbid version of the Gjallarhorn, this silver-bound ivory war-horn is often outlawed in &quot;civilized&quot; Consilli. When blown, it causes any corpses within a [Scale] area around the sounder to animate under her control. Any obvious signs of their undeath are masked for the duration, papering over wounds and decongealing blood. <hr /><br /> <b>Imbued Item</b>: &quot;The&quot; Gjallarhorn, AKA The Avernian Horn (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Effects</b>: Create Avernian Gate (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Mana Cost</b>: 2<br /> <b>Mana Reservoir</b>: 3<br /> <b>Activation</b>: Contingent (The horn is sounded)<br /> <b>Reach</b>: Advanced Duration<br /> <b>Other Traits: </b>No Flexible Reach, Relinquished, Time In A Bottle, Everywhere<br /> <br /> Forged of weathered brass, it is traditional to engrave the words &quot;The Grave Is No Bar To My Call&quot; around the mouth of these horns in a dead language or High Speech.<br /> <br /> Boasting one of the oldest known Gjallarhorns amongst their number, The Avernian Horns are \u200brelatively simple in function but require a great deal of preparation to use. When blown, they rip open an Avernian Gate where the sounder stands, the Iris always leading to a specific Underworld realm tied to that particular horn. Owners who do not perform their due diligence may see a scant handful ghostly marauders arrive on the scene, but those who prepare can call up legions of the dead. The fact that these allies will not be affected by Dissonance usually makes up for the fact that the hornsounder will need to have negotiated their services beforehand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 04-02-2023, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T01:21:18-07:00","id":1506933,"title":"","content":"Legacy seed - &quot;wand&quot; using, potion-brewing witch.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Prime/Matter, and primarily want to make use of <u>Word of Comman</u>d, &quot;<u>Create Tass</u>&quot;, and <u>Spell Potion</u>. The Disciple-level practitioners would basically end up being potion-sellers, with their exact repertoire depending on their other Arcana. Life would likely end up being very popular.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it feels a lot like I'm just remaking the Eyes of Ein Sof.<br /> <br /> Initiate<ul><li><u>Word of Command</u> (Instant Casting)<ul><li>Use &quot;wands&quot;</li> </ul></li> <li>Detect Substance (Instant Casting, factors to Scale)</li> </ul>Apprentice<ul><li><u>Supernal Vision</u> (Advanced Duration, Instant Casting)? <u>Scribe Grimoire</u> (Instant Casting, Lasting)?<ul><li>SV is basic, but reliable.</li> <li>SG is... boring, and kinda pointless. Maybe make it be able to &quot;copy&quot; existing Grimoires? That way they can peddle cantrips even if they don't know them.</li> </ul></li> <li><u>Craftsman's Eye</u> (Instant Casting, &quot;How to Use&quot;, Permanence)<ul><li>Limited to potential ingredients or tools for crafting potions, food, candles, or other consumables.</li> </ul></li> </ul>Disciple<ul><li>&quot;<u>Create Tass</u>&quot; (Advanced Duration)<ul><li>Based on Mana Battery. Spend an hour creating a consumable, which grants Mana when consumed. Atypical - costs no Mana to activate, but stored Mana is drawn from the Legacy member's own pool upon creation.</li> </ul></li> <li><u>Spell Potion</u> (Advanced Duration)<ul><li>Same as the above, and can be activated simultaneously. Stored spells don't take up Spell Control, as long as the Legacy member is the one infusing them.</li> </ul></li> </ul>Adept<ul><li><u>Dispel Magic</u> (Instant, Sight, Lasting)? <u>Wards and Signs</u> (Instant, Duration, Potency to Primary)?<ul><li>Boring, if reliable options.</li> </ul></li> <li>???</li> </ul>Master<ul><li>???</li> <li><u>Golem</u>? (Instant Casting, Advanced Duration) Only works on Spell Potions created with the Disciple Attainment?</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 04-02-2023, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T09:14:04-07:00","id":1506955,"title":"","content":"Is this a Moros legacy? You could try and pull inspiration from SoS Stygian section on Prime, I find it very evocative. I see could see the legacy being very different than the Eyes by focusing on Tass as a catalyst.<br /> <br /> As for the various attainments, Detect Substance could be good for the first for getting rare materials for potions. As for the second, Craftsman's eye with the reach for how to use the object is the way to go, lets one know how to use any artifact or substance they come across. Very useful for a magic item focused legacy. I should note that you can make &quot;potions&quot; from certain materials like drugs to produce various effects on the body, by enhancing various properties. Bet that gets weird when that's Tass with unusual properties.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about the Pseudo-Demesne, I've always felt that's more for legacies that tie themselves to a specific location. Something like putting themselves into the land. Now making a pseudo soul stone feels more in line with the Magical item maker feel, which can then be leveraged into a Demesne if you want, or a super golem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T02:29:15-07:00","id":1507169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1506955#post1506955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a Moros legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hadn't decided yet, but the alchemical bent of them -and Matter being the Optional Arcana- would make them the best choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the various attainments, Detect Substance could be good for the first for getting rare materials for potions. </div> </div> </div>Aye. I was hoping for a direct tie to the Prime side, but that's probably the best choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the second, Craftsman's eye with the reach for how to use the object is the way to go, lets one know how to use any artifact or substance they come across. Very useful for a magic item focused legacy. I should note that you can make &quot;potions&quot; from certain materials like drugs to produce various effects on the body, by enhancing various properties. Bet that gets weird when that's Tass with unusual properties. </div> </div> </div>Probably have it be a rider on the <u>Supernal Vision</u> then. A pity, I kinda wanted to make <u>Scribe Grimoire</u> an Attainment for the heck of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure about the Pseudo-Demesne, I've always felt that's more for legacies that tie themselves to a specific location. Something like putting themselves into the land. Now making a pseudo soul stone feels more in line with the Magical item maker feel, which can then be leveraged into a Demesne if you want, or a super golem. </div> </div> </div>Guess I was leaning into the witch-y stereotypes, where you don't challenge Baba Yaga in her cabin. Maybe not then. The Matter capstone being the ability to Golemize any spell poition might be fun - health potions that force themselves down your throat if you've passed out, that kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T14:10:20-07:00","id":1507214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1507169#post1507169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably have it be a rider on the <u>Supernal Vision</u> then. A pity, I kinda wanted to make <u>Scribe Grimoire</u> an Attainment for the heck of it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think you still can. Craftsman\u2019s Eye should reveal enough Supernal Properties, especially with a Prime Component to get by.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1507169#post1507169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess I was leaning into the witch-y stereotypes, where you don't challenge Baba Yaga in her cabin. Maybe not then. The Matter capstone being the ability to Golemize any spell poition might be fun - health potions that force themselves down your throat if you've passed out, that kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, you meant that kind of witch. Oh, Golem is perfect then, just go with dolls, creepy effigies, and wax skulls rather than stone or metal.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T14:23:27-07:00","id":1507218,"title":"","content":"What about <i>Shaping</i>, being able to hide your potions anywhere, repairing your cabin or sinking an unruly visitor into the floor seems fitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T16:19:15-07:00","id":1518788,"title":"","content":"So, two Cults I cobbled together for the heck of it. Not sold on the rank-naming scheme for either if anyone has any suggestions. Or general suggestions/criticism, I'm not picky.<br /> <br /> For the Web of Civilization, I toyed a bit with giving them the Fixer merit instead of Eidetic Memory, but I generally don't want to give merits that participants aren't guaranteed to qualify for. Having the first tier of Mystery Cult give a dot of Professional Training would give them the Contacts dots necessary, but you generally shouldn't combine MC and PT as far as I'm aware. Likewise, the Citywalker Merit from Core might be interesting, but it's mortal-only. Plus I like the idea that Citywalking crops up as an unintended effect of them disrupting their own patterns.<br /> <br /> <b>The Web of Civilization</b> <i>Mystery Cult (Independent, Formerly God-Machine)</i><br /> <br /> Civilization spreads across the land, single points in the wilderness that expand outwards. Slowly at first, cutting a new trail between two settlements to facilitate trade. Then faster and faster, exponentially increasing with every new point on the web. Eventually civilization covers the land, sustained by trade networks and the infrastructure to support them.<br /> <br /> That growth has given rise to The Web of Civilization, a Mystery Cult of merchants and logisticians who tend to the great arteries and networks through which the lifeblood of civilization flows. Where the Cult's influence is strongest, those pathways form strange symbols and tangled runes. Profit is never the goal - the perpetuation of civilization is.<br /> <br /> Low-ranking members are often members of vital -if simple and often under-appreciated- professions such as truck drivers, warehouse workers, or longshoremen, but higher ranks are not limited to CEOs and the wealthy. Cult activities mostly revolve around keeping trade open and flowing - war profiteers are ironically one of the few areas the Web encourages violent action against. War may be good for buisness, but it's awfully hard on infrastructure.<br /> <br /> The Web of Civilization has existed in several forms across the ages, often as several concurrent but unaffiliated cults in different parts of the world. The earliest verifiable records of the Cult date back to Venice in the early 740s, though hearsay has them cropping up as early as Harappa. The Web's most cohesive and continuous cell originated in the early days of the Iroquois Confederacy, Peacemaker's legacy focusing on trade as cooperation more than profit. It has spread across the North American continent since that time, jumping cultures as needed but remaining a singular organization. The branches of Asia have often been larger or more influential, but have merged and fractured with alarming regularity.<br /> <br /> During the British Raj, a majority of the Cult's branches were verifiably Stigmatic pawns of the God-Machine. Under the GM's influence the Cult's more esoteric practices began to standardize, with their incidental geoglyphs drifting towards a convergent pattern. Even after the GM inexplicably withdrew its influence during the Cold War era, the Cult has continued to make heavy use of the memory-enhancing ritual that it mandated all Junctions undergo.<br /> <br /> \u25cf <u>Filiment</u> - Gain the Specialty Academics (Logistics)<br /> \u25cf\u25cf <u>Intersection</u> - Gain the Area of Expertise (Logistics) Merit, or the Good Time Management Merit<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <u>Junction</u> - Gain the Eidetic Memory Merit, the Web's more esoteric training regimens allowing the initiate to recall reams of manifests at the drop of a hat.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <u>Anchor</u> - Gain three dots of Status to allocate towards organizations that make significant use of logisticians - a nation's military or mail service, Amazon, UPS, etc<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <u>Network</u> - Gain three dots of Resources, representing strategic supply-chain investments and/or lucrative contracts<br /> <br /> Secrets and Storyhooks<ul><li>The ritual to promote a new Junction is one of the few overtly supernatural aspects of the Web of Civilization - the candidate is sedated using a special cocktail of nootropics and sedative extracts, and placed in a room laden with maps, trade data, and manifest records. Other members of the cult form a circle around the subject, and begin a deep, wordless chant. The one Mage who has studied the process reported that the room was spontaneously flooded with Astral Resonance, and that <i>something</i> temporarily entered the subject's Onieros from the deep Tenemos. While the entity quickly departed, the new Junction's Onieros showed subtle structural changes that appeared to correlate to their now-eidetic memory.</li> <li>The Web's geoglyphs are difficult to pick out amidst the general tangle of urbanization, but there are distinct &quot;dialects&quot; in every region of the world. When those dialects transition on a gradient, things run smoothly. When dialects from halfway across the world mingle, however, strange glitches such as city-walking begin to crop up. A potentially useful tool... if not for the increase in encounters with the Crossways Abyssal Entity.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>The Custodians of Progress AKA &quot;Free Technologies, LLC&quot;</b><br /> <i>Mystery Cult (Pantechnion, Web of Pain)</i><br /> <br /> The Custodians are Pantechnion pawns through and through, dedicated to commoditization of invention and innovation. Through their front as Free Technologies, the Cult advocates for looser copyright and patent restrictions, while also offering technological consultation to stalled R&amp;D projects. Though the former often makes companies leery of working with the LLC, their track record with having the <i>exact</i> bit of data needed to make a project viable often drives individual researchers to their doors. Especially when their initial fees are so low!<br /> <br /> Of course, once Free Technologies has helped you perform a miracle, it's so easy to keep going back. And if they occasionally ask for project data, in lieu of their steadily increasing consulting fees? Well, it's not like they can intergrate proprietary tech without getting hauled into court, right?<br /> <br /> The Custodians maintain an extensive archive of R&amp;D projects and data from across the globe, and seek to expand that archive to encompass as much of human innovation as possible. To that end, they seed or seduce agents in various corporations and universities, infiltrating labs via research assistants and boardrooms via the secretary pool. The actual scientists within the cult reap great rewards off the work of their peers, creating more advanced technological leaps through the amalgamation of disparate projects.<br /> <br /> Though popular with the civilian population who have heard of them, Free Technologies generally stays out of the headlines. Their activities are often contested by TELM Trust, who represent one of the few organizations that the Custodians are actively rivals with.<br /> <br /> Though the Cult perpetuates an internal image of being visionaries building a physical Akashic Record, their origin is far less glamorous than the rank and file know. When a Pantechion Prelate known now as Cycle attained Archmastery in the late 1990s, her aponia resulted in a child she didn't remember having. Uninterested in the child as anything beyond a Mystery to study, she set up the Custodians as a kind of guardianship for her newfound offspring. Sold to the rest of the Ministry as a tool for commoditization of intellectual progress, the Custodians and their charge are largely ignored unless a Seer needs to aquire intel on a corporation's R&amp;D department. Some vast spell Cycle worked into the cult's charter keeps the company below notice, although unfortunately for individual agent this only applies at the organizational level.<br /> <br /> The Tetrarch conveys her will to the cult through the mouth of her child, and has made it abundantly clear to the Cynosures that their continued prosperity and direction lasts only as long as their oracle lives. Free Technologies' board of directors have invested a great deal of resources towards that end, up to and including the creation of several Deviants to act as bodyguards and handlers.<br /> <br /> \u25cf <u>Vibration</u> - Gain the Specialty Science (Theory Appraisal)<br /> \u25cf\u25cf <u>Cascade</u> - Gain a dot in Contacts (R&amp;D), representing the Cult's network of scientists and developers who've benefited -often &quot;fortuitously&quot;- from consultations with Free Technologies<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <u>Tulpa</u> - Gain the Eidetic Memory Merit, to better facilitate extracting sensitive data<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <u>Akashic</u> - Gain three dots of the Library (Science) Merit, representing access to the Cult's accumulated store of data and research<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <u>Cynosure</u> - Gain three dots of Resources, representing income from various patents and discoveries.<br /> <br /> Secrets and Storyhooks<ul><li>The process a Tulpa undergoes to gain their Eidetic Memory was the product of research culled from several Conspiracies within the Web of Pain. Of course, the research that eventually Perfected the process lead to a <i>staggering</i> amount of Deviants, mostly of the Cephalist Clade.</li> <li>Given that a great deal of their research draws from the Web of Pain, it's not surprising that Free Technologies is responsible -directly or indirectly- for Renegade cohorts. Some are even intentionally aided or released into the wild, for both study and the opportunity their sabotage on other Conspiracies can bring. Invasives and Chimerics see the highest rates of utilization, but Coactives infused with Supernal or Abyssal energies are unusually common within the cult's own labs</li> <li>The Cult's oracle shows up at the local TELM office, newly Awakened and asking for sanctuary and training. Apparently there's been infighting on the Ministerial level, and Cycle engaged in a mutual kill with a Paternoster Tetrarch directly in front of the now slightly traumatized cult idol. The stress -and sheer Supernal saturation of the fight- seems to have drawn the attention of one of the Watchtowers. With Cycle gone, the Cult has no direct Seer influence, and her oracle is surprisingly reticent to go to the Ministries. Control -albeit indirect- of the Custodians is being offered, but how far can the offer be trusted?</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-25-2023, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T20:54:01-07:00","id":1518805,"title":"","content":"What's a good 5-dot benefit for a Mystery Cult of Fae ecologists? I'm thinking a bunch of Mages decided that understanding Arcadia is the key to Ascension, and started an Occult research group. Mages typically get fast-tracked to the 3rd tier, with Sleepers/Sleepwalkers doing a lot of the grunt work.<br /> <br /> The things I've considered so far are:<ul><li>Library 3 (Occult) - kinda boring</li> <li>Faction Member 3 (Invisible Path) - makes a certain amount of sense, but a little odd</li> <li>Retainer 3 or Allies 3 - have it be Hobs or Changelings? Kinda boring</li> <li>Grimoire 3 - Stack it with Mind and/or Fate spells. Boring, but very practical</li> <li>Astral Adept - <i>something somethin</i>g entering the Hedge is like entering the Astral <i>something something</i></li> <li>Spend a point of Mana to open existing Hedgegates without needing to cast a spell - not aweful. Means you don't need to be a Fate Mage to make your own way into the Hedge. On the other hand, not having Fate in the Hedge is a bit of a bad idea.</li> </ul><br /> Faecologists Mystery Cult (Pentacle)<br /> \u25cf Gain the Specialty Occult (Changelings)<br /> \u25cf\u25cf Gain the Interdisciplinary Specialty (Changelings) Merit<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Gain the Perfected Item merit, representing a Siderite-Hermium-Lunargent amalgam amulet given to trusted initiates. As long as the item is worn against the skin, the initiate also gains the benefit of the Unseen Sense (Fairies) Merit. The amulet begins to vibrate when in the presence of something with a Wyrd rating or a Mask, though this becomes useless when in the Hedge.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Gain three dots of the Occultation Merit, the Mage having learned to insulate themselves metaphysically from both the Wise and the Wyrd. Only Mages may reach this level.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf ???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-26-2023, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T11:23:25-07:00","id":1518833,"title":"","content":"What is normal? Could you grant them Hollow merit (essentially like Sanctum but within the Hedge).<br /> <br /> A three dot merit, or access to a collective Hollow which multiple members use in a given area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T14:19:50-07:00","id":1518845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1518833#post1518833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is normal? Could you grant them Hollow merit (essentially like Sanctum but within the Hedge).<br /> <br /> A three dot merit, or access to a collective Hollow which multiple members use in a given area?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad suggestion. Not quite feeling it tho.<br /> <br /> Eh. I'll go with this for now.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Gain three dots of the Grimoire merit. At least half of the encoded Rotes must be of the Mind and Fate Arcana, typically related to Changeling and The Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-26-2023, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T23:04:50-07:00","id":1519157,"title":"","content":"I have the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1484955#post1484955\">Pure Sovereigns written up here</a>, but imma make another version on this thread<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pure Sovereigns</b><br /> The Sovereigns are a Ladder Legacy based around mastering body and mind through intense internal control. The underlying principles rely on the idea that Mind and Life are deeply intertwined, and that by only controlling one you fail to truly utilize the whole. Once you understand how your body works, it's easy to use it effectively, or even apply that understanding to others.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization: </b>Bluebloods tend to be ambitious, but cooperate readily as a Legacy when goals align. Most Bluebloods prefer to focus primarily on master-student relationships, with several acolytes working under the direction of a senior instructor. On the other hand, Bluebloods tend to drift towards Cabals with complementary Legacies, such as the Sisterhood of the Blessed. Consilli with influential Sovereigns will often have a Cryptopoly based around their body-control exercises, a surprisingly reliable source of Sleepwalker assistants that endears the Legacy to their peers.<br /> <b>Theory:</b> Before one can master the world, one must master one's self.<br /> <b>Background:</b> (See the 1e book Silver Ladder for official fluff.) A Legacy of mages focused on self-mastery, with a history that extends back into antiquity. Though exact origins are spotty, they are generally accepted as a cousin of the Perfected Adept family of Legacies, possibly a Silver Ladder variation that has gained sufficient independence to become it's own tradition. Major lines of impeccable pedigree have been recorded in the British Isles, Nepal, and India, but the practice has become diffuse enough that it isn't tied to any region.<br /> <br /> Modern practitioners have often made jokes about the similarities between themselves and the Bene Gesserit of the Dune novels. This has begun to influence the Cryptopolies Sovereigns run, with references to Gom Jabbars and Spice Agony appearing in the rhetoric particularly flippant cult-managers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Parentage:</b> Silver Ladder; Mastigos, Thyrsus<br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Life. Thyrsus instead gain Mind<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Being surrounded by faithful attendants (+1), interpretive dancing or full-body mudras representing the spell (+2), mentoring lesser beings through the use of, or supported by the use of, the spell (+2), enforcing order (+1), benevolent ministration (+2), emotionally-resonant oration (+2)<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Exercise katas; dictating your significant thoughts to your attendants; mentoring lesser beings<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Life 2, Mind 1; at least one dot in Athletics or Brawl; at least one dot in Science, Medicine, or Occult; at least one dot in Empathy, Expression, Socialize, or Subterfuge; Specialty (Body Control) in one of the previously listed Skills<br /> <b>Initiation: </b>Initiation into the Sovereigns requires that a prospective member gain a sense of bodily awareness that exceeds normal pain-and-pleasure responses. Often this requirement is met simply by joining a Sovereign Cryptopoly, but it is not unheard of for unaffiliated practitioners to develop their own methods. Usually achieved through specific exercises, a prospect will eventually reach a point where they can optimally filter their sensory input - not just experience temperature, touch, sight or sound, but sort those data streams into usable conclusions. A successful prospect will reach a tipping point, where the optimization becomes instinctive and automatic and the first Legacy Marks scribe onto their Gnosis. A common superstition is that practicing the exercises in a Demesne or other place of power will accelerate the process, but cautious mentors claim this can have odd effects.<br /> <br /> Achieving the Blood of Silver is little different from the Mind of Amber, and more often than not a Blueblood achieves both refinements simultaneously. The exercises involved are more extensive and full-bodied, but are frequently taught concurrently because they combine disparate lower-level movements. The rigors of this process serve to unify the flow of physical and psychological feedback loops, making it difficult to shift one without the other.<br /> <br /> Achieving the Flesh of Gold is a harrowing experience. Some practitioners are exposed to increasingly intense toxins and illnesses, some are subjected to overwhelming pain that is not caused by actual physical damage. Ultimately, the Sovereign must exercise their bodily understanding to repair what they can, purge what they must and ignore what they cannot change. Flippant practitioners often refer to this as the Gom Jabbar test, and set up the ceremony to ape it.<br /> <br /> Achieving the Incarnation of Thunder is highly introspective. Every Sovereign eventually begins to wonder what the limits of their bodily control is, and the quest to find these limits is in of itself the process to scribe their Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Those rare texts that detail how to achieve The Sage Ascendent describe it in painful terms, involving strange concoctions and tumultuous Astral journeys. Occasionally called &quot;The Spice Agony&quot;, little is known about the process beyond the fact that a Sovereign will be forced to confront something deep in the Temenos realm of their Legacy. Some claim it is the accumulated memories of their predecessors, others that it is a Goetia Manifestation of the practitioner's &quot;genetic memories&quot;, and still others that it is a spark of knowledge left behind by the lost Kings of Atlantis. Whatever the truth, Sage Sovereigns manifest prowess with mundane skills that few humans can match unaided.<br /> <br /> <b>Special:</b> Thanks to the increasing control over -and optimization of- their biology, each level of initiation slows the Blueblood's aging by half. That is, an Initiate would only age a day for every two that pass, a Disciple would age a day for every eight, and a Master would age a day for every 32. This is just a rule of thumb - exact biology may vary between practitioners, and generally none of it will come up in play.<br /> <br /> <i>Mind of Amber </i>\u25cf<br /> (Life \u25cf, Mind \u25cf) <u>Initiation</u><br /> Though a human's senses are somewhat pathetic by the standards of the animal kingdom, a great deal is simply lost due to insufficient processing power. The Pure Sovereign's first refinement eases that limitation, enhancing their natural faculties for both perception and comprehension. They add [Potency] Dice to Perception rolls.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Heightened Senses<br /> Potency= Lower of Life and Mind<br /> Duration = Lasting<br /> Casting Time = N/A<br /> Range = Self<br /> NOTE: Consider allowing the player to purchase a Survival Specialty to track by scent alone</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Refining the flow of information within mind and body also gives the Sovereign a deeper understanding of how the two halves interact. By careful optimization, the Blueblood can separate out their consciousness into parallel streams, one housed in grey matter and the other in pure psyche.<br /> <br /> The Blueblood can take an additional Instant Action, or sustain an Extended Action, each turn. However, said action must primarily take place within their mind. Actions that rely on external inputs, such as Perception or Empathy rolls, are acceptable, but a separate task with each hand is not.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">One Mind Two Thoughts <br /> Duration = Lasting<br /> Potency = N/A<br /> Casting Time = Lasting<br /> Range = Self<br /> <br /> Simulfow and 1e both dictate this Attainment, though it's actually coming in pretty early this edition.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Blood of Silver </i>\u25cf\u25cf<br /> (Life \u25cf\u25cf, Mind \u25cf\u25cf) <u>Interdisciplinary Specialty (Body Control)</u><br /> To progress beyond being a mere initiate, a novice Blueblood practices a routine of precise, deliberate movements passed down to them by their master. They advance into Apprenticehood in the moment they finally execute the routine perfectly, the Blueblood becoming acutely aware of the inner workings of their body. By fine-tuning these processes, the Blueblood refines the efficiency of even their most humble cells.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Body Control<br /> Potency = Lower of Life and Mind<br /> Duration = Lasting<br /> Casting Time = N/A<br /> Range = Self<br /> NOTE: Gains both Reach effects.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> The first step to self-mastery is to tame the body. The second step is to tame the mind. The two halves work as a seamless whole, and invasive attempts to alter one create a dissonance in the other. Bluebloods are able to shrug off external attempts to affect his emotions or control him, his limbic system or psyche re-asserting the natural order if their counterpart is assaulted. This absolute control has a secondary benefit, allowing the Blueblood to select their current emotional state as an Instant Action. Furious? Extinguish the rage. Unhappy? Will it away. Sad? Put a smile on that face (and soul).<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Mental Shield/Emotional Urging<br /> Duration = Lasting (Two Reach to Lasting)<br /> Potency = N/A (2, 3 at Mind 4)<br /> Casting Time = N/A<br /> Range = Self<br /> NOTE: Clash of Wills uses [lower of Life and Mind + Gnosis]. It explicitly does <i>not</i> protect against mind/emotion reading. Changing your own emotions does not trigger PMS<br /> <br /> Alternative - use the Deviant power <u>Superhuman Resolve</u>'s 3-Magnitude special ability, using the lower of Life and Mind in the Clash of Wills.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>Flesh of Gold </i>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> (Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) <u>Trained Observer 1 and a</u><u>t least 6 dots spread in any combination amongst the Initiation Skills</u><br /> The Bluebloods strive to exemplify Thunder - self-sufficient paragons that inspire others to seek the Imperium. To do so they must be seen as unassailable, shrugging off physical travails with but a moment's thought. Even more than other Life-focused Mages, the Sovereigns are masters of self-healing and bodily control.<br /> <br /> This has several benefits;<ul><li>The Blueblood's accelerated healing from <i>Blood of Silver</i> now also applies to Aggravated damage</li> <li>The Blueblood can use Pattern Restoration to repair Resistant Damage, and can heal Aggravated damage at a rate of 3 Mana per health level</li> <li>The Blueblood is automatically aware of any poisons, toxins, or diseases entering or affecting their body, and automatically provokes a Clash against Supernatural efforts to cloak such intrusions</li> <li>The Blueblood can take a Instant Action to force a resistance roll against any disease or poison they are aware of that is currently affecting them, consciously directing their biology to combat intrusion</li> <li>The Blueblood adds their dots in Life to all rolls to resist disease and poison, and Exceptional Successes on such rolls only require three successes, rather than five. An Exceptional Success purges the offending condition outright, even if it would normally be incurable.</li> </ul><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Forcing the roll does not trigger PMS. A combination of a bunch of different things - <u>Purge Illness, Cleanse the Body,</u> and a bit of <u>Mend</u>, at a minimum. Maybe Always-On Life Mage Sight focused on their own body? Anyway, Blood of Silver is already boosting Bashing and Lethal healing and a brace of resistances, and &quot;self healing&quot; is the theme I chose to emphasize, so I don't think it particularly breaks anything.<br /> <br /> Plus, it's more or less what their 1e incarnation got at this level.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> A young Sovereign's understanding of their own physiology responses gives them great insight into the minds of others. A more advanced Sovereign has sufficient understanding and self-mastery to begin &quot;mastering the world&quot;.<br /> <br /> By modulating their pitch, tone, and word choice to trigger limbic responses, the Sovereign may issue short, one-to-two-word commands to all human and human-adjascent entities within earshot. This works as if they had cast Psychic Domination, but the Sovereign must be clearly heard and understood by the target. If the Sovereign focuses on a single specific target, they may instead tailor their modulation to issue a complex, sentence-long command as if having used the first Reach effect.<br /> <br /> This Attainments does not trigger Peripheral Mage Sight or provide immediate knowledge that the target is being unnaturally commanded, though hostile targets may become suspicious if they abruptly accommodate their Blueblood foe.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Psychic Domination<br /> Potency = Lower of Life and Mind<br /> Withstand = Resolve<br /> Duration = 2 turns, 3 Turns at Mind 4<br /> Casting Time = Instant<br /> Range = Sensory<br /> NOTE: Earshot Area &quot;Advanced Scale&quot; if using a simple order, &quot;Complex Orders&quot; Reach effect if focused on a single target.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>Incarnation of Thunder</i> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> (Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) <u>Trained Observer 3, least 8 dots spread in any combination amongst the Initiation Skills</u><br /> The Blueblood's mastery of the self has begun to flower - by engaging in a deep meditative trance, they are now able to reshape themselves into their humanist ideal. This is no mere deceptive mask thrown across an imperfect framework, but instead the assertation that their form is a nascent Supernal Truth.<br /> <br /> The Blueblood's accelerated healing also benefits, allowing them to regrow teeth, organs, and limbs. Mark the health box that caused Persistent Conditions such as Blind or Crippled, as if they were Arm/Leg Wrack, and resolve them in the same way. Unless killed outright, they are capable of recovering from <i>anything.</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Many Faces<br /> Potency = Life<br /> Duration = Lasting<br /> Casting Time = Scene<br /> Range = Self<br /> NOTE: Doesn't need Time 3 to affect apparent age. Each activation changes the caster's &quot;default&quot; form.<br /> <br /> Plus something close to Regeneration</div></div> </div> </div><br /> A Sovereign of Thunder needs little rest, and can heal their mind as easily as their flesh. A successful meditation roll is treated as a full night's rest, and restores a point of Willpower. The Sovereign can also resolve up to [Mind] Mental Conditions or Tilts, though they gain no Beats for doing so.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Clear Thoughts<br /> Potency = Mind<br /> Duration = Lasting<br /> Casting Time = Ritual<br /> Range = Self<br /> NOTE: &quot;Willpower&quot; Reach, &quot;Lasting&quot; Reach<br /> <br /> No exact parallels anywhere (except maybe a DnD Elan). But I like it, it feels like it fits the theme</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>The Sage Ascendent </i>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> (Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) <u>Astral Adept, Eidetic Memory, and at least 10 dots spread in any combination amongst the Initiation Skills</u><br /> The Blueblood's physical and mental perfection has more or less blossomed - even in a task they have never attempted, their every action is suffused with competence. Some claim the Sovereign is tapping into genetic memory, others that they are drawing knowledge from the Astral, but the Legacy remains tight-lipped.<ul><li>The Sovereign never suffers untrained penalties, and is always considered to have a single dot in every Skill in which he has no dots.</li> <li>Once per Scene, until the end of the scene, the Sovereign is considered to have three dots in a single Skill of the player\u2019s choice.</li> <li>Once per chapter, until the end of the scene, the Sovereign is considered to have three dots in every Skill in which he has fewer than three dots</li> <li>Once per chapter, until the end of the scene, the Sovereign is considered to have five dots in a single Skill of his player\u2019s choice</li> </ul>Any Skill dots gained from this ability do not count for the purposes of learning Specialties or Merits.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Omnicompetence. Will you go hard into Attributes, leaning on your connection to the Astral? Or will you be your own person?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Legacy Secrets and Story Hooks</b><br /> \u25cf Mages with an understanding of the Chrysalides Legacy sometimes wonder if there is a connection between the two traditions. Did the first Swan arise as a way to keep Seers with body dysmorphia in the fold? Was the first Sovereign a disgusted response by the Silver Ladder when the first Swan became known to them?<br /> <br /> \u25cf Sovereigns gain great health and power through their institutional exercises, and often set up Cryptopolies teaching truncated versions to Sleepers. This becomes a problem when a trigger-happy foreign Guardian begins investigating an outbreak of Flesh Intruders in the area. Believing them to be practicing Sinister Organ Qigong, the Guardian begins a campaign against the local Sovereigns, using methods both subtle and overt. Whether the Guardian is <i>right</i> is up to the Storyteller. Are the Pure Sovereigns as a whole, in fact, less &quot;Pure&quot; than they claim?<br /> <br /> \u25cf A Daimonomikon titled &quot;The 25 Purities Path&quot; has surfaced in the Consillium. Some young, impulsive Mages have used it to initiate themselves into what seems to be a Pure Sovereigns lineage, but are rapidly falling into self-mutilating madness. Is the Daimonomikon cursed, flawed, or a trap? Or do the erstwhile initiates simply need a proper mentor to help them see their &quot;imperfections&quot; as flaws to be corrected rather than cancers to be excised?<br /> <br /> \u25cf It has become well-known that Flesh of Gold Sovereigns can force others to obey them with but a word, and that traditional cues do not make such commands obvious. Now, the Consillium is blaming any inconvenience or poor decision on Blueblood influence. Is this just a natural reaction to a somewhat concerning ability, or is someone actively driving a wedge into the Pentacle?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Typical Blueblood Cryptopoly</b><br /> Promoting themselves as a holistic wellness organizations, these cults often attract middle-managers and office worker who are dissatisfied with their sedentary lifestyle. The most advanced cultists are able to brush at the barest edges of the Astral, approaching the Sovereign's Tenemos Realm through a lens of &quot;genetic memory&quot;<br /> \u25cf Gain Specialty (Body Control) in Medicine, Athletics, Empathy, Expression, or Subterfuge<br /> \u25cf\u25cf Gain the Interdisciplinary Specialty (Body Control) Merit<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Gain the Eidetic Memory Merit<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Gain three dots of the Trained Observer Merit<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Gain the Astral Adept Merit if a Sleepwalker or Mage, or three dots of the Dream Merit if a Sleeper. If the latter, they may choose to convert those dots into the Astral Adept Merit if they ever Awaken or go through a change that would normally make them a Sleepwalker","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-07-2024, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T21:13:12-08:00","id":1525289,"title":"","content":"Scribblings of a Moros Mind Legacy. I have the powers of the first two tiers about where I want them, but not much else. The Apprentice tier reads a lot like the Uncrowned Kings, in that the Uncrowned got both those powers in 1e. I can see a couple of ways to go with it.<br /> On the one hand, an always-on sense of human-level intellects nearby screams &quot;paranoia&quot; to me. It's a broad utility, but it would probably have a <i>lot</i> of use for spies. Similarly, <u>Soul Marks</u> would be good for identifying what entities are in the area - you'd have to concentrate on a specific subject every turn to learn specific information, but that would make it perfect for something like Project Nightfall. Identify the enemy agents, and eliminate. Taken from that perspective, later tiers should emphasize stealth and misdirection, which would drift them into something similar to the Subtle Ones. Or possibly the Quiessent, for a less goal-driven paranoid.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it could just be a straight-up monster hunter. I'm iffier on what later-tier powers would be then - choosing a specific brand of enemy to fight would be best, but even just working on the basis of them being Th\u00e9archs who are <i>viscerally offended</i> by the amount of entities out there who maim human souls gives the idea more direction. Dedicated combatants of the Tremere, maybe?<br /> <br /> In either case, the Apprentice powers are just pragmatic.<br /> <br /> Initiate<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Mind 1<br /> Mind version of &quot;Web of Life&quot;<br /> Duration = Lasting<br /> Potency = N/A<br /> Scale = House, Small Warehouse at Mind 2, Large Warehouse at Mind 4<br /> Range = Self<br /> Casting Time = N/A<br /> NOTE: Web of Life, only it detects human-comparable intelligence. Cannot detect entities who have at least one Mental Attribute above 5. Rule of thumb: Ephemeral Entities below Rank 3 are usually too under-developed to be detected.<br /> <br /> Death 1<br /> Soul Marks<br /> Potency = Lower of Death and Mind<br /> Duration = N/A (1 Turn)<br /> Range = &quot;Sensory&quot;<br /> Casting Time = Instant<br /> NOTE: Can only target subjects detected by the Mind portion, but can do so even if the target is not in line of sight.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Apprentice<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Mind 2<br /> Mental Shield<br /> Duration = Lasting<br /> Potency = N/A<br /> Range = Self<br /> Casting Time = N/A<br /> <br /> Death 2<br /> Soul Armour<br /> Duration = Lasting<br /> Potency = N/A<br /> Range = Self<br /> Casting Time = N/A<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Spy/Paranoia Route:</b><br /> On the one hand, <u>Alter Mental Pattern</u> is pulling double-duty with <u>Mental Shield</u>. On the other, having two lines of defense against mental intrusions is a good thing. The question then is whether the AMP is layered <i>on top</i> or the MS, or if AMP <i>itself</i> is the secondary defense.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, the Ticktock Men had something similar in 1e... so another question would be whether to have it be an always-on power with one fixed personality, that keeps &quot;reacting&quot; in the manner that personality would be expected to. Probably not, that would work better in the Legion of the Lost or the actual Ticktock Men. Plus, the relevant Ticktock Men were full-on Abyssals.<br /> <br /> <u>Surpress Aura</u> is mostly a counter-espionage power in this context. Keeps other supernaturals from identifying them. Plus, if I'm reading the spell right, it also subtracts dice from attempts to pierce AMP. Again, always-on might be neat, but that Empathy penalty would probably be detrimental in the long-term. Hard for people to trust someone they can't read.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Mind 3<br /> Alter Mental Pattern<br /> Potency = Mind<br /> Duration = 1 Day, 1 Week at Mind 4<br /> Range = Self<br /> Casting Time = Instant<br /> <br /> Death 3<br /> Surpress Aura<br /> Duration = Death<br /> Potency = N/A<br /> Range = Self<br /> Casting Time = Instant<br /> NOTE: Can be activated simultaneously with the Mind portion.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Adept is a bit late to be getting around to <u>Incognito Presence</u> and <u>Machine Invisibility</u>, but they're also <i>goddamn useful</i>. Especially in tandem. The Optional requiring Matter is probably the more correct choice, especially if it's a Moros Legacy, but I also like the idea of their mastery of Death just... fuzzing out any surveillance on them. Not actually make them invisible, but rather make them into a horror movie monster who turns the screen to static whenever they enter the field of view. Which might actually be a <i>disadvantage</i> in some scenarios- that Temple Guardian Golem might be intelligent enough to start punching in the general vicinity of where their vision keeps failing.<br /> <br /> <u>Cut Threads</u> would also be a viable Optional.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Mind 4<br /> Incognito Presence<br /> Potency = Mind<br /> Duration = One Week<br /> Range = Self<br /> Cost = 1 Mana<br /> Casting Time = Instant<br /> NOTE: Potency to Primary<br /> <br /> Death? Matter? 4<br /> Machine Invisibility<br /> Duration = Death (Advanced Duration)<br /> Potency = N/A<br /> Range = Self<br /> Casting Time = Instant<br /> NOTE: Can be activated simultaneously with the Mind portion. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the capstone would be. There's plenty of old fallbacks for Mind - <u>Psychic Domination</u>, <u>Read the Depths</u>, <u>Hallucination</u>, etc. But none really jump out at me, nor much for the Optional. <u>Empty Presence</u> and <u>Forge No Chains</u> might be a good combo, but A) this isn't a Death-primary Legacy, and B) the Adept tier is already doing a lot of the same stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>Any Other Route</b><br /> I have a jumble of possible stuff, but a lot of it isn't cohesive.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>For a Death Optional at the Disciple tier, maybe make Death Armor's effects be constantly on, and able to stack with other kinds of Mage Armor? Death Mage Armor is the only one that doesn't directly add to your Defense (and thus scale with your Arcana), iirc. Maybe have the Mind side reduce wound/fatigue penalties in some way? Combined, the tier would have a &quot;my body is just a shell I pilot&quot; feel</li> <li>Attack spells in the Adept slot, Bashing-tier but able to be done at Sight Range. Combined spells. You ever think about how deadly combined attack spells are, even un-Attainmentized? It's pretty much doubling your damage for only a -2 penalty, for the tradeoff of not being able to use Rotes.</li> <li><u>Mental Scan</u>, only usable against things detected by the Initiate? Might be useful, dunno what would be a good Optional.</li> <li><u>Sever Soul</u> might be interesting, but that's a pretty Legacy-defining power to have in the Optionals. And I have no idea what would be a good main-track pairing, beyond maybe <u>Possession</u> or a really callous application of <u>Read the Depths</u>.</li> <li>A non-spell equivalent power? I keep thinking of the Arcane Curse for Sidereals in Exalted, but that's a <i>big</i> thing.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-10-2023, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T23:07:54-08:00","id":1525293,"title":"","content":"Looking at the path where they specialize on counterintelligence, <i>Perfect Recall</i> could be a helpful first optional Attainment, it fits the Guardian's tradition of transmitting key information exclusively orally, it also allows them to recall any scenario perfectly, allowing them to further scrutinize it. <i>Without a Trace</i> could be used instead of <i>Soul Armor</i>, ensuring their hair, fingerprints and similar are not left behind as evidence. <br /> <br /> <i>Ghost Gate</i> with the Reach option would allow them to bypass any mundane surveillance.<br /> <br /> The capstones could be <i>Social Networking</i> and <i>Empty Presence</i>. So now these spooks can modulate how much attention they draw. They can be a known threat that can just show up anywhere, easily integrate into any social structure and vanish. But if things get difficult, they can go into deep cover, eliminating themselves from the board so completely that their enemies shift priorities, allowing them to choose the perfect moment to strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T08:48:52-08:00","id":1525309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1525293#post1525293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the path where they specialize on counterintelligence, <i>Perfect Recall</i> could be a helpful first optional Attainment, it fits the Guardian's tradition of transmitting key information exclusively orally, it also allows them to recall any scenario perfectly, allowing them to further scrutinize it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose, but Mind is the main track, and the Eidetic Memory Merit covers a lot of the same ground. Having that Merit as a Prerequisite maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Without a Trace</i> could be used instead of <i>Soul Armor</i>, ensuring their hair, fingerprints and similar are not left behind as evidence. </div> </div> </div> I like it, and it was a consideration, but how do I tie it back to the Mind portion? <u>Mental Shield</u>+<u>Soul Armor</u> can be spun as extending MS's Subtle protection, but creating a permanent personal bubble of entropy is a bit more disconnected. It would be good paired with <u>Incognito Presence</u>, though that means it's a choice between it and <u>Machine Invisibility</u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Ghost Gate</i> with the Reach option would allow them to bypass any mundane surveillance. </div> </div> </div> I suppose. <u>Shadow Flesh</u> would also fill that niche, and I'm trying to lean away from the &quot;Ghost&quot; side of Death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The capstones could be <i>Social Networking</i> and <i>Empty Presence</i>. So now these spooks can modulate how much attention they draw. They can be a known threat that can just show up anywhere, easily integrate into any social structure and vanish. But if things get difficult, they can go into deep cover, eliminating themselves from the board so completely that their enemies shift priorities, allowing them to choose the perfect moment to strike. </div> </div> </div>That works really well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T16:16:26-08:00","id":1556577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1497861#post1497861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate:<ul><li>Any &quot;lucker&quot; spell. That is, stuff like <u>Quantum Flux</u>, which eliminate penalties, and <u>Exceptional Luck / </u><u>Superlative Luck</u> which add dice or give Rote qualities.<br /> EL makes an OK Apprentice Attainment with either Instan Casting or Advanced Duration, or as an Adept Attainment if your ST allows the &quot;spellcasting roll&quot; Reach.<br /> SL makes a good Disciple or Master Attainment, using the exact same logic as EL.</li> <li><u>Serendipity</u> as an Disciple Attainment (Instant Casting, &quot;Any Skill&quot;) will make you into a true McGuyver - in any mundane scenario, you can immediately twist thing around to a Skill of your strength.<br /> As an Apprentice Attainment (Instant Casting, &quot;Same Skill Group&quot;), you're still skilled, but still limited based on what your skill-spread is. Making it Scene Casting, &quot;Same Skill Group&quot; is still useful, but you can't do it on the fly.<br /> As an Initiate, it's a good way to become a minor prophet or detective, regardless of if you make it Instant Cast or &quot;Same Skill Group&quot;</li> <li><u>Fools Rush In</u> isn't as useful as the stuff above, but it still keeps you from being at a disadvantage in most scenarios.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Apprentice <u>Shifting the Odds</u> is effectively useless without Advanced Duration. I'd either swap it and <u>Warding Gesture</u> around to bump it up a slot, or make it Scene-cast, Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <u>Chaos Mastery</u> is fine, but <u>Miracle</u> is actually less useful than it seems at first glance. Because of how little reach you have to work with, <u>Miracle</u> is basically going to be <u>Chaos Mastery</u> again. And both suffer from &quot;Touch/Aimed&quot; syndrome. In general, I find that the best spells for a given slot come from a practice at least one level lower; Adept spells are usually better in the Master slot than Master spells, Disciple spells over Adept spells in the Adept slot, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is your opinion on <i>Sworn Oaths</i> at Adept level? Instant Casting, Advanced Duration. You can buff yourself with boons (9-again on every skill roll, potence bonus to any skill roll, lots of favourable conditions) as often as you need it, and you can dispel the attainment forgoing the boon but also the hex if your boon is no longer applicable... Without counting the Clash of wills to avoid being stopped from doing something your really want.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}